{{~##
   One record type, at one level of indent.

   Included from two places and written once, because the type is the same shape wherever
   it is declared: a group nobody declared gets it beside the table's record, and a group
   a `.tbs` file typed gets a file of its own.
   spec/types/declared-struct-identity.md.
##~}}
struct {{ rt.type_name }} {
{{~ for member in rt.members ~}}
{{~ for line in member.comment ~}}
  /// {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ for line in member.declarations ~}}
  {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~## The per-target accessors of every member of this struct that reaches several tables. One
   taking the element number where the member is the array, which is the third place an element
   number sits. spec/references/multi-target-accessors.md. ##~}}
{{~## The second layer of a container's surface. The vectors above are the file's order; these
   are the lookup, and neither of this language's hash containers keeps one.
   spec/types/set-and-map.md section 7. ##~}}
{{~ for line in rt.lookups ~}}
  {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
};
